IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s388-domestication`

-- Tests of dg11-s388-domestication.l4 (section 388). Expected values are worked by hand from the text of the section and written beside each assertion.

-- A fixture: a corporation formed abroad. The core's `a corporation` carries the Kind of corporation under this chapter (section 114(d)); a non-United States
-- corporation is not organized under this chapter, so the field is a fixed placeholder that no rule here reads.
`a non-United States corporation` MEANS `a corporation` WITH `its kind` IS `a stock corporation`

§ `Section 388(a) - definitions`

#ASSERT NOT `s 388(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `this State`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `another jurisdiction of the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
-- every kind of entity the definition lists is a non-United States entity if formed under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a non-United States corporation` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a statutory trust` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a business trust or association` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a real estate investment trust` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a common-law trust` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a general partnership` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a limited partnership` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a limited liability partnership` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a limited liability limited partnership` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a joint-stock association` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `any other unincorporated business or association` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
-- a natural person is not an entity of any of those kinds
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a natural person` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
-- formed in this State or in another jurisdiction of the United States: not a non-United States entity
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a limited liability company` `this State`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` `a non-United States corporation` `another jurisdiction of the United States`

§ `Section 388(b), (g), (h) - becoming domesticated`

-- The filing, by position: certificate of corporate domestication executed per (g); it is filed per § 103; certificate of incorporation executed, acknowledged and filed per § 103; filed simultaneously;
-- to be effective on filing, as § 103(d) permits; each provides for the same effective date or time.
`a filing effective on filing` MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a filing with the same later effective date` MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a filing with neither` MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a filing not simultaneous` MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a filing with the domestication certificate not executed per (g)` MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a filing with the domestication certificate not filed per section 103` MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a filing with the certificate of incorporation not filed per section 103` MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Arguments: kind of entity; where formed; has complied with (h)?; the filing.
#ASSERT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing effective on filing`
#ASSERT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing with the same later effective date`
-- the certificates are not to be effective on filing and do not provide for the same effective date or time
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing with neither`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing not simultaneous`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing with the domestication certificate not executed per (g)`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing with the domestication certificate not filed per section 103`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing with the certificate of incorporation not filed per section 103`
-- (h) not complied with
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` FALSE `a filing effective on filing`
-- not a non-United States entity
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a limited liability company` `this State` TRUE `a filing effective on filing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` `a natural person` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE `a filing effective on filing`

-- (g): signed by any person authorized to sign on behalf of the entity
#ASSERT `s 388(g) the person may sign the certificate of corporate domestication` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(g) the person may sign the certificate of corporate domestication` FALSE

-- (h): approved in the manner provided, before the certificate becomes effective, and the certificate of incorporation by the same authorization
#ASSERT `s 388(h) the domestication has been approved as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(h) the domestication has been approved as required` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(h) the domestication has been approved as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(h) the domestication has been approved as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 388(c) - the certificate of corporate domestication`

-- By position: (1) date and jurisdiction of first formation; (2) name immediately before; (3) name of the corporation; (4) seat or principal place of business; (5) approval before effectiveness; (6) plan approved.
`a certificate certifying (1) to (5)` MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a certificate certifying (1) to (6)` MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a certificate lacking (1)` MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a certificate lacking (2)` MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a certificate lacking (3)` MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a certificate lacking (4)` MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a certificate lacking (5)` MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

-- Arguments: what the certificate certifies; a plan of domestication is adopted?
#ASSERT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate certifying (1) to (5)` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate certifying (1) to (6)` TRUE
-- (6) is needed only if a plan is adopted
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate certifying (1) to (5)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate lacking (1)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate lacking (2)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate lacking (3)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate lacking (4)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` `a certificate lacking (5)` FALSE

§ `Section 388(d) to (f)`

-- (d): both certificates effective
#ASSERT `s 388(d) the non-United States entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State, and the corporation is subject to all of the provisions of this title` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(d) the non-United States entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State, and the corporation is subject to all of the provisions of this title` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(d) the non-United States entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State, and the corporation is subject to all of the provisions of this title` FALSE TRUE
-- existence is deemed to have commenced when the entity first came into being abroad (here 17 May 1990), not on the filing
#ASSERT `s 388(d) the date on which the existence of the corporation is deemed to have commenced` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1990 5 17) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1990 5 17)
#ASSERT `s 388(d) the date on which the existence of the corporation is deemed to have commenced` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1990 5 17) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (e)
#ASSERT `s 388(e) the domestication leaves the matter unaffected` `an obligation or liability of the non-United States entity incurred prior to its domestication as a corporation in this State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(e) the domestication leaves the matter unaffected` `the personal liability of a person for such an obligation or liability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(e) the domestication leaves the matter unaffected` `another matter that s 388(e) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (f): before the effective time the choice of law is unaffected; from it, Delaware law applies
#ASSERT `s 388(f) the law that applies to the entity at the time in question` FALSE EQUALS `the choice of law that applied to it before the filing, unaffected by the filing`
#ASSERT `s 388(f) the law that applies to the entity at the time in question` TRUE EQUALS `the law of the State of Delaware, including this title, as if it had been incorporated as a corporation of this State on that date`

§ `Section 388(i), (j)`

#ASSERT `s 388(i) the corporation is deemed to be the same entity as the domesticating non-United States entity, a continuation of its existence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(i) the corporation is deemed to be the same entity as the domesticating non-United States entity, a continuation of its existence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the domestication has become effective?; the entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction?
#ASSERT `s 388(i) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the non-United States entity remain vested` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the corporation alone`
#ASSERT `s 388(i) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the non-United States entity remain vested` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the corporation and also the non-United States entity, if and for so long as it continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`
#ASSERT `s 388(i) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the non-United States entity remain vested` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(i) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the non-United States entity remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the corporation alone`
#ASSERT `s 388(i) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the non-United States entity remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the corporation and also the non-United States entity, if and for so long as it continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`
#ASSERT `s 388(i) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the non-United States entity remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(i) title to real property vested in the non-United States entity reverts or is impaired by reason of this title` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(i) title to real property vested in the non-United States entity reverts or is impaired by reason of this title` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(i) the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of the non-United States entity are preserved unimpaired` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(i) the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of the non-United States entity are preserved unimpaired` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(i) the rights, privileges, powers, interests in property, debts, liabilities and duties are deemed to have been transferred to the corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(i) the rights, privileges, powers, interests in property, debts, liabilities and duties are deemed to have been transferred to the corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (j): arguments: otherwise agreed?; applicable non-United States law otherwise requires?
#ASSERT `s 388(j) the domestication requires the domesticating non-United States entity to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(j) the domestication requires the domesticating non-United States entity to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(j) the domestication requires the domesticating non-United States entity to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(j) the domestication is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the non-United States entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(j) the domestication is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the non-United States entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(j) the corporation and the non-United States entity constitute a single entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(j) the corporation and the non-United States entity constitute a single entity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 388(k), (l), (m)`

#ASSERT `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into cash in a domestication` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into property in a domestication` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into shares of stock, rights or securities of the corporation in a domestication` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another corporation or other entity in a domestication` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `cancelled in a domestication` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `treated in a way that s 388(k) does not name` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `cancelled in a domestication` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `the terms and conditions of the domestication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `the mode of carrying the same into effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `that the certificate of incorporation of the domesticated corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan of domestication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the non-United States entity, in accordance with subsection (k)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `any corporate action to be taken by the domesticated corporation of this State in connection with the domestication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `any details or provisions as are deemed desirable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `such other provisions or facts as shall be required by the laws of the jurisdiction under which the non-United States entity is organized` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `a statement that s 388(l) does not list` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(l)(v) the corporate action stated in the plan may be taken` TRUE
-- the "facts" sentence: an event, and a determination or action by any person or body, are facts; a fact of another kind is not shown not to be one
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `the occurrence of any event` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `a determination or action by any person or body, including the non-United States entity or the domesticated corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `a fact of another kind that s 388(l) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(l)(v) the corporate action stated in the plan may be taken` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) a term of the plan of domestication may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(l) a term of the plan of domestication may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` FALSE
-- (m): arguments: set forth in a plan approved in the manner provided by (l)?; within the power of a corporation under subchapter II?
#ASSERT `s 388(m) the action is deemed authorized, adopted and approved, and needs no further action of the board of directors, stockholders or members under this title` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(m) the action is deemed authorized, adopted and approved, and needs no further action of the board of directors, stockholders or members under this title` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(m) the action is deemed authorized, adopted and approved, and needs no further action of the board of directors, stockholders or members under this title` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the certificate under another section must say so
#ASSERT `s 388(m) the certificate meets the requirement of the last sentence of subsection (m)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(m) the certificate meets the requirement of the last sentence of subsection (m)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(m) the certificate meets the requirement of the last sentence of subsection (m)` FALSE FALSE
